From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arseniy Velikanov <me@adomerle.pw>
Date: Thu, 17 Jul 2025 07:20:59 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: mtk-mutex: Defer until the mutex device has
 probed

mtk_mutex_get() dereferences the mutex device's driver data, which is
NULL until that device has probed. With mediatek-drm and the mutex
probing in either order, a CRTC created first oopses. Return
-EPROBE_DEFER instead.

Signed-off-by: Arseniy Velikanov <me@adomerle.pw>
[Patrick: from linux-mediatek mt6789-next 3e6c84ec8051; commit message]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-mutex.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-mutex.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-mutex.c
index 38179e8c..2308e3de 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-mutex.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-mutex.c
@@ -850,6 +850,9 @@ struct mtk_mutex *mtk_mutex_get(struct device *dev)
 	struct mtk_mutex_ctx *mtx = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int i;
 
+	if (!mtx)
+		return ERR_PTR(-EPROBE_DEFER);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < MTK_MUTEX_MAX_HANDLES; i++)
 		if (!mtx->mutex[i].claimed) {
 			mtx->mutex[i].claimed = true;
